# Checked direction.md and sessions.jsonl first. druid:feral has nine prior
# sessions (walk/clear/raid/daily/battleground, styles idle/good/auto/dodge/
# flee/mash) but mode=clear + style=auto + 25-heroic + carried + this exact
# tall-portrait-tablet viewport (820x1180,touch) has never been run: the one
# style=auto evening on record for this spec (mode=walk, boss=skyward,
# 25-heroic, carried) used 844x390,touch -- a short landscape phone, not this
# tall portrait one. This matters for #386 (AUTO toggle's hit-circle eating
# ability:4/5 on narrow touch) and #387 (ability-cluster self-overlap): both
# were measured mostly on narrow viewports, and #387's own comments already
# confirmed the overlap is viewport-independent at 390/844/1280 widths but
# NOT yet checked at 820px tall-portrait. Also: "clear" is judged by whether
# the evening reaches a wing's end page, for each of the four wings -- no
# druid:feral session has ever been run long enough (room budget) to see
# past THE VIGIL, since the one prior mode=clear for this spec+style+size+
# difficulty combo doesn't exist and most other specs' clear attempts spend
# their whole budget stuck in THE VIGIL per direction.md hypothesis 6.
